Unicode-aware palindrome check that ignores case and punctuation:

```rust
fn is_palindrome(text: &str) -> bool {
    let chars: Vec<char> = text
        .chars()
        .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric())
        .flat_map(|c| c.to_lowercase())
        .collect();
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = chars.len();
    while i + 1 < j {
        j -= 1;
        if chars[i] != chars[j] {
            return false;
        }
        i += 1;
    }
    true
}

fn main() {
    for s in ["A man, a plan, a canal: Panama", "Résumé", "abc", ""] {
        println!("{:?} -> {}", s, is_palindrome(s));
    }
}
```

Empty strings return true, and `to_lowercase` expands Unicode so accented characters compare correctly.

