`getchar` returns an `int` so `EOF` is distinguishable from every byte value; storing it in a `char` would break the loop on input containing 0xFF. A trailing line without a newline is not counted as a line, matching the `wc -l` convention. Spaces, tabs, and newlines all terminate a word because `isspace` covers them.

