Iterating over `input.chars()` yields scalar values, so multi-byte code points are handled without slicing on byte boundaries. `HashSet::insert` returns `false` for a repeat, which lets `filter` do the dedup in one pass with O(n) time and O(k) space. The final string is built by `collect`, preserving first-occurrence order.

