```rust
fn longest_common_prefix(words: &[String]) -> String {
    if words.is_empty() {
        return String::new();
    }
    let first = words[0].as_bytes();
    let mut len = first.len();
    for w in &words[1..] {
        let b = w.as_bytes();
        len = len.min(b.len());
        let mut i = 0;
        while i < len && first[i] == b[i] {
            i += 1;
        }
        len = i;
        if len == 0 {
            break;
        }
    }
    words[0][..len].to_string()
}

fn main() {
    let a = vec![String::from("flower"), String::from("flow"), String::from("flight")];
    let b: Vec<String> = vec![];
    let c = vec![String::from("dog"), String::from("cat")];
    println!("{:?} {:?} {:?}", longest_common_prefix(&a), longest_common_prefix(&b), longest_common_prefix(&c));
}
```

The prefix length only shrinks, so each comparison is bounded; slicing `words[0][..len]` is safe because `len` never exceeds the byte length of the first word. For UTF-8, comparisons are byte-wise which is correct for finding a common prefix as long as you slice at a char boundary — here `len` always lands on a boundary of `first` because matches are byte-equal.

