        print(repr(c), "->", repr(longest_palindrome(c)))
```

Expand-around-center runs in O(n^2) time and O(1) extra space. Empty input returns `""`, and a single character is its own palindrome. The even-length branch (`expand(i, i + 1)`) is what catches `"bb"` in `"cbbd"`.

