After each erase the cursor `pos` stays put, so the next `find` starts where the removed text began. That makes removal non-overlapping: `"aaaa"` with `"aa"` yields `""` in two passes rather than leaving a stray `"aa"`. An empty needle is returned unchanged to avoid an infinite loop.

