```rust
fn longest_run(bytes: &[u8]) -> usize {
    let mut best = 0usize;
    let mut current = 0usize;
    let mut prev: Option<u8> = None;
    for &b in bytes {
        if prev == Some(b) {
            current += 1;
        } else {
            current = 1;
            prev = Some(b);
        }
        if current > best {
            best = current;
        }
    }
    best
}

fn main() {
    assert_eq!(longest_run(b""), 0);
    assert_eq!(longest_run(b"a"), 1);
    assert_eq!(longest_run(b"aaabbbbaa"), 4);
    assert_eq!(longest_run(b"abc"), 1);
    println!("ok");
}
```

`prev` remembers the last byte and `current` counts the run it belongs to. Resetting `current` to 1 on a change (not 0) is what makes the first byte of a new run count. The empty slice never enters the loop and returns 0. `best` is updated each step so no second pass is needed.

