`x &= x - 1` clears the lowest set bit each iteration, so the loop runs exactly once per set bit rather than once per bit position. Base 0 in `strtoull` accepts decimal, `0x` hex, and octal, and malformed arguments are reported and skipped instead of silently parsed as 0.

