    puts("ok");
    return 0;
}
```
Each `x &= x - 1` clears the lowest set bit, so the loop runs exactly once per set bit — O(popcount) rather than O(64). The run is verified against `0xFF` (8 bits), `UINT64_MAX` (64 bits) and a two-bit value.

