The loop tracks the previous two values in `a` and `b`. Before each addition it checks `UINT64_MAX - a < b`, which is a subtraction-safe test for unsigned overflow. For `n = 93` it prints `fib(93) = 12200160415121876738`; at `n = 94` it reports `overflow at n=93` instead of wrapping silently.

