`min(..., key=len)` picks a reference string so the loop never runs past the shortest input. The inner loop scans each string at index `i`; the first mismatch returns the prefix built so far. Empty input returns `""` because `min` would raise on an empty sequence. Unicode works because Python compares code points element-wise.

