    cases = ["babad", "cbbd", "", "a", "forgeeksskeegfor", "ünnü"]
    for c in cases:
        print(repr(c), "->", repr(longest_palindrome(c)))
```

Expand-around-center runs in O(n²) worst case but uses O(1) extra memory, unlike the DP table which needs O(n²) space. It handles empty input, single characters, and unicode correctly since Python indexes code points, not bytes.

