Here is an expand-around-center implementation. It checks every center (single character and between characters) and keeps the longest match, running in O(n^2) time and O(1) extra space.

```python
def longest_palindrome(s: str) -> str:
    if not s:
        return ""

    def expand(left: int, right: int) -> str:
        while left >= 0 and right < len(s) and s[left] == s[right]:
            left -= 1
            right += 1
        return s[left + 1:right]

    best = ""
    for i in range(len(s)):
        odd = expand(i, i)
        even = expand(i, i + 1)
        for candidate in (odd, even):
            if len(candidate) > len(best):
                best = candidate
