`operator>>` on a stream skips leading whitespace and reads up to the next whitespace, so runs of spaces and tabs collapse naturally and empty tokens never appear. `getline` reads the whole line first so the input is not split on newline instead of spaces. An input of only spaces produces zero words, which the program reports rather than looping forever.

