        print("no numeric values found")
    else:
        print(f"mean = {mean:.4f} ({skipped} rows skipped)")
```

It uses `csv.DictReader` so column lookup is by header name rather than position, and reports how many rows were discarded instead of silently dropping them. A missing column raises a clear `KeyError` naming the available headers.

