```cpp
struct Node {
    int value;
    Node* next;
};

Node* reverse(Node* head) {
    Node* prev = nullptr;
    Node* cur = head;
    while (cur) {
        Node* next = cur->next;
        cur->next = prev;
        prev = cur;
        cur = next;
    }
    return prev;
}
```

We walk the list once, saving `next` before rewiring `cur->next`. When the loop ends `prev` points at the old tail, which is the new head. An empty list returns `nullptr`.

