    parts = s.split(".")
    if len(parts) != 4:
        return False
    for part in parts:
        if not part.isdigit():
            return False
        if len(part) > 1 and part[0] == "0":
            return False
        if not 0 <= int(part) <= 255:
            return False
    return True
```

Each octet must be all digits, no leading zeros unless it is exactly "0", and within 0-255. This rejects things like `192.168.1.256` and `01.2.3.4`.

