`lo + (hi - lo) / 2` avoids the signed overflow that `(lo + hi) / 2` can hit. The loop condition `lo <= hi` and inclusive `hi` give the standard half-open-by-one invariant, and an empty vector yields `hi = -1` so it returns -1 immediately.

