```rust
/// Returns (F(n), F(n+1)) with checked arithmetic.
fn fib_pair(n: u64) -> Option<(u128, u128)> {
    if n == 0 {
        return Some((0, 1));
    }
    let (a, b) = fib_pair(n / 2)?;
    let c = a.checked_mul(b.checked_mul(2u128)? - a)?; // F(2k) = F(k)*(2F(k+1)-F(k))
    let d = a.checked_mul(a)?.checked_add(b.checked_mul(b)?)?; // F(2k+1)
    if n % 2 == 0 {
        Some((c, d))
    } else {
        Some((d, c.checked_add(d)?))
    }
}

pub fn fib(n: u64) -> Option<u128> {
    fib_pair(n).map(|(a, _)| a)
}

fn main() {
    assert_eq!(fib(0), Some(0));
    assert_eq!(fib(10), Some(55));
    assert_eq!(fib(100), Some(354_224_848_179_261_915_075));
    assert_eq!(fib(200), None); // overflows u128
    println!("ok");
}
```

Fast doubling gives O(log n) multiplication steps. Every multiplication and addition goes through `checked_*`, so a result past `u128::MAX` returns `None` instead of wrapping. `fib(200)` is roughly 2.8e41, well beyond the u128 ceiling near 3.4e38.

