The comparison `b[j] < a[i]` (rather than `a[i] <= b[j]`) picks from `a` on ties, which keeps the merge stable; equal elements retain their relative order. Empty and duplicate-heavy inputs are covered, and `reserve` avoids reallocations during the merge.

