`T acc{}` value-initialises the accumulator, so integer and floating-point types both start at zero and empty vectors yield 0 correctly. The size mismatch throws `std::invalid_argument` rather than reading out of bounds. The template works for any type with `operator*` and `operator+`, and `std::size_t` avoids signed/unsigned comparison warnings in the loop.

