Each opening bracket is pushed and each closing bracket must pop a matching opener, so an empty stack at the end means balance. Checking `st.empty()` before popping guards the lone-closer case, and mismatched pairs like `([)]` fail because the top of the stack is the wrong opener. Non-bracket characters are skipped, which lets mixed text pass through.

