Two indices walk inward; non-alphanumeric bytes on either side are skipped. `unsigned char` casts avoid undefined behaviour from `isalnum`/`tolower` on negative `char` values. On multibyte UTF-8 input the byte-level comparison is only a heuristic, which is noted rather than hidden.

