    assert merge_intervals([(5, 6), (1, 2)]) == [(1, 2), (5, 6)]
    print(len(merge_intervals([(1, 3), (2, 6), (8, 10)])))
```

Intervals are sorted by start then end, and each new interval either extends the last merged one or starts a new block. Touching intervals like `(1,4),(4,5)` merge because the check is `start <= merged[-1][1]`; an empty list returns `[]` rather than raising on the first index.

