`low` holds the smaller half as a max-heap, `high` the larger half as a min-heap. After every insert we rebalance so their sizes differ by at most one. The median is `low.top()` when odd, or the mean of both tops when even. If stdin is empty, `low` stays empty and we print `no input` instead of reading an empty heap.

