Filtering then `flat_map(to_lowercase)` handles multi-char lowercase mappings and non-ASCII letters. `saturating_sub` keeps the empty string from underflowing `len() - 1`. Two-pointer scan is O(n) after collection.

```rust
fn fib(n: u32) -> Option<u128> {
    let (mut a, mut b) = (0u128, 1u128);
    for _ in 0..n {
        let next = a.checked_add(b)?;
        a = b;
        b = next;
    }
