The `-printf '%f\n'` prints only basenames so a file like `src/config.yaml` contributes `.yaml`, not the whole path. The regex `\.[^.]+$` finds the last dot in the name, which means `archive.tar.gz` counts as `.gz` and a name with no dot falls into `(none)`. `sort -rn -k1,1` ranks by numeric count descending; the final `awk` reformats the output. Invoke it as `./count_ext.sh ~/src`. On systems with GNU find `-printf` (Linux) this works directly; on macOS/BSD find, replace the find line with a `for` loop or install GNU find via coreutils.

