        if (low.empty() || x <= low.top()) low.push(x);
        else high.push(x);

        if (low.size() > high.size() + 1) {
            high.push(low.top());
            low.pop();
        } else if (high.size() > low.size()) {
            low.push(high.top());
            high.pop();
        }

        double median = (low.size() == high.size())
                            ? (low.top() + high.top()) / 2.0
                            : static_cast<double>(low.top());
        std::cout << median << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Run with `echo "5 1 3 2" | ./median`. The max-heap holds the smaller half, the min-heap the larger half; after each insert we rebalance so sizes differ by at most one. Median is the top of `low` when odd, or the average of both tops when even. No input means no output, which is correct.

