    size_t count = sizeof(samples) / sizeof(samples[0]);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        printf("%lld -> %s\n", samples[i], is_prime(samples[i]) ? "prime" : "not prime");
    }
    return 0;
}
```
The `i * i <= n` bound stops at the square root without calling `sqrt`. Testing candidates 6k±1 skips multiples of 2 and 3, which is roughly three times fewer divisions than testing every integer. Values below 2, including negatives and 0 and 1, are rejected immediately.

