    std::vector<int> expected{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8};
    assert(merge_sorted(a, b) == expected);
    assert(merge_sorted({}, {}) == std::vector<int>{});
    assert(merge_sorted({1, 1}, {1}) == (std::vector<int>{1, 1, 1}));
    std::cout << "ok\n";
    return 0;
}
```

The `<=` keeps the merge stable for duplicates, `reserve` avoids reallocations, and the trailing `while` loops flush whichever vector still has elements. Empty inputs are handled by the loop guards.

